cff-version: 1.2.0
title: IteratedFiniteAutomaton
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Pavel
    family-names: Hajek
    affiliation: Wolfram Institute
abstract: >-
  Iterated finite automata and automata groups: evolution, periodicity, state
  analysis, and conversion between Mealy and wreath recursion formalisms, based
  on Andrzej Zuk's WSRI26 essay. Includes a catalog of nineteen open problems in
  group theory paired with the automaton statements that would settle them.
keywords:
  - iterated finite automaton
  - Mealy automaton
  - automata group
  - self-similar group
  - wreath recursion
  - rooted tree
  - group ring
  - Kaplansky conjecture
  - Burnside problem
  - Wolfram Language
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/WolframInstitute/IteratedFiniteAutomaton
references:
  - type: article
    title: Iterated Finite Automata
    authors:
